        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "6. When we peruse the averments made in the PIL petition, what we find is that not even a single act amounting to offences as narrated in the letter dated 30th June 2022 is mentioned to have been committed by the private respondents."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "cf810f72bdfc48949e16672e81d8c6dc_16",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "By impleading 902-CRPILST.23688.2023 certain celebrities in different walks of life in the society, the petitioner appears to be seeking publicity instead of taking the issue with expected seriousness."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "8f933406213a440b9b612ffe46b05c05_17",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "7. Hon'ble Supreme Court in the case of State of Uttaranchal vs. Balwant Singh Chaufal & Ors.,\nreported in (2010) 3 SCC 402 has clearly observed that the Court should, on one hand, encourage the PIL petitions being filed raising genuine pub"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "fe6f5aa4ebbe49eda70d7261e7c55a3e_18",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The observations made in the said judgment are as follows: -\n181."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "aa1ca10aa08045de9c4f07193b67a70b_19",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "We have carefully considered the facts of the present case."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "2fe897ea31b34bbcbe51c559b39d82f6_20",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "We have also examined the law declared by this Court and other courts in a number of judgments."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "12ec0910d0f44d6cbb52782b4aca77ff_21",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\nIn order to preserve the purity and sanctity of the PIL, it has become imperative to issue the following directions:\n(1) The Courts must encourage genuine and bona fide PIL and effectively discourage and curb the PIL filed for extraneous c"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "679a7c0ee22346869297ae9d7a461759_22",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\n(2) Instead of every individual Judge devising his own procedure for dealing with the public interest litigation, it would be appropriate for each High Court to properly formulate rules for encouraging the genuine PIL and discouraging the "
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "612b1280cd7c45d0ac1e55b5d0997008_23",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Consequently, we request that the High Courts who have not yet framed the rules, should frame the rules within three months."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "925d8b1c4f074fa9b47a159e2beee9ba_24",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\nYash Foundation vs Union Of India And Ors on 8 May, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/167704076/\n2"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "ea33fefb9ca04d649cb462c7bee42fce_25",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The Registrar General of each High Court is directed to ensure that a copy of the rules prepared by the High Court is sent to the Secretary General of this Court immediately thereafter."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "36daf897ab704924bc88493353fe26e2_27",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\n(5) The Courts should be fully satisfied that substantial public interest is involved before entertaining the petition."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "fe08772aac274d3eb07cbd20d88a442b_28",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\n(6) The Courts should ensure that the petition which involves larger public interest, gravity and urgency must be given priority over other petitions."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "c8328fb611344b178582d2768ee5da8a_29",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\n(7) The Courts before entertaining the PIL should ensure that the PIL is aimed at redressal of genuine public harm or public injury."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "af4ce610ecb84ea1960eabd068da4d7e_30",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The Court should also ensure that there is no personal gain,\nprivate motive or oblique motive behind filing the public interest litigation."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "77bc6e16373d4a2eaf7ea1f7a1b20ac3_31",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\n(8) The Courts should also ensure that the petitions filed by busybodies for extraneous and ulterior motives must be discouraged by imposing exemplary costs or by adopting similar novel methods to curb frivolous petitions and the petitions"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "b951cb254b21401dbef835753adc98c0_32",
        "summary_section": "decision",
        "labels": [
          "RPC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:decision",
          "forbidden_labels:RPC",
          "suspicious_label:rpc"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "8. However, at the request of the learned counsel for the petitioner, we are not going into the aforesaid issues in the matter, but we find it appropriate to caution the petitioner that in future if it files any PIL petition, it should firs"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "11b2cabfc4e0471aac632978d5fa8138_33",
        "summary_section": "decision",
        "labels": [
          "RPC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:decision",
          "forbidden_labels:RPC",
          "suspicious_label:rpc"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
